From c909a11220f69c99a34044bd68dc3e3af96e2d94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 03:41:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] fix(allwinner): support key-protected watchdogs in
 SYSTEM_RESET

The H713/sun50iw12 watchdog uses the sun55i-style key-protected
register layout: CFG at +0x10, MODE at +0x14, and every write is
ignored unless bits [31:16] carry the 0x16aa key. The generic reset
sequence (v1.0 layout at +0x14/+0x18, no key) is therefore a silent
no-op and PSCI SYSTEM_RESET falls through to panic().

When the platform defines SUNXI_WDOG_KEY (sun50i_h713 does, in its
sunxi_mmap.h), write the keyed CFG/MODE sequence instead. Verified on
the HY200 board: U-Boot's 'reset' now warm-reboots the full chain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 28abd3c67..ca82284c5 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -54,10 +54,21 @@ static void __dead2 sunxi_system_reset(void)
 {
 	gicv2_cpuif_disable();
 
+#ifdef SUNXI_WDOG_KEY
+	/*
+	 * Key-protected watchdog layout (H713/sun50iw12): CFG at +0x10,
+	 * MODE at +0x14, writes ignored without the 0x16aa key.
+	 */
+	/* Reset the whole system when the watchdog times out */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0010, SUNXI_WDOG_KEY | 1);
+	/* Enable the watchdog with the shortest timeout (0.5 seconds) */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0014, SUNXI_WDOG_KEY | 1);
+#else
 	/* Reset the whole system when the watchdog times out */
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG, 1);
 	/* Enable the watchdog with the shortest timeout (0.5 seconds) */
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, (0 << 4) | 1);
+#endif
 	/* Wait for twice the watchdog timeout before panicking */
 	mdelay(1000);
 
